  "problem": "In a cinema, a snack combo consists of four hot dogs, two medium fries, and two medium soft drinks. The cost of one hot dog is $H$ dollars, the cost of one portion of fries is $F$ dollars and the cost of one drink is $D$ dollars. Alan is purchasing some combos for his friends and the total bill comes to $5(4H+2F+2D)$ dollars. \n\nWhat does the factor $5$ mean in this context?",
  "worked_solution": "A hot dog costs $H$ dollars, one medium fries costs $F$ dollars, and a medium soft drink costs $D$ dollars. Thus, the cost, in dollars, of a combo is\n\n$$\n4H+2F+2D.\n$$\n\nAlan's bill, in dollars, comes to\n\n$$\n5(4H+2F+2D).\n$$\n\nHence, the factor $5$ must be the total number of combos that he's purchased.",
